<rss version="2.0" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><title>智能新闻| smithsonianmag.com</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/rss/smart-news/</link><description>智能新闻的 RSS 提要</description><lastBuildDate>Mon, 21 Sep 2026 02:06:39 GMT</lastBuildDate><generator>rfeed v1.1.1</generator><docs>https://github.com/svpino/rfeed/blob/master/README.md</docs><item><title>月球刚刚出现了一个巨大的新陨石坑，比两个足球场还要宽。这是一次“一生一次的观察”</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-moon-just-got-a-massive-new-crater-thats-wider-than-two-end-to-end-football-fields-its-a-once-in-a-lifetime-observation-180989526/</link><description>这个撞击坑形成于 2024 年，当时一个多层建筑大小的物体撞上了我们的月球伴侣。由此产生的草皮大约 728 英尺宽、141 英尺深</description><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 19:04:38 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-moon-just-got-a-massive-new-crater-thats-wider-than-two-end-to-end-football-fields-its-a-once-in-a-lifetime-observation-180989526/</guid></item><item><title>一群 40 个真人大小的野牛木偶将于本周末穿越纽约，以纪念原住民的历史和坚韧</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-herd-of-40-life-size-bison-puppets-will-stampede-through-new-york-this-weekend-to-honor-indigenous-history-and-resilience-180989525/</link><description>这些巨大的牛，每头都由三名木偶操纵者操纵，将在曼哈顿下城和布鲁克林漫步</description><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 18:44:15 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-herd-of-40-life-size-bison-puppets-will-stampede-through-new-york-this-weekend-to-honor-indigenous-history-and-resilience-180989525/</guid></item><item><title>几个世纪前，一位建筑师将帕台农神庙的曲线描述为一种巧妙的视错觉。现在，一位数学家提出不同意见</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/centuries-ago-an-architect-characterized-the-parthenons-curves-as-a-clever-optical-illusion-now-a-mathematician-begs-to-differ-180989520/</link><description>公元前一世纪，维特鲁威写道，卫城最大的神庙是水平弯曲的，这样它就不会下垂，这种解释持续了数千年。新研究提出了不同的原因</description><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 17:11:29 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/centuries-ago-an-architect-characterized-the-parthenons-curves-as-a-clever-optical-illusion-now-a-mathematician-begs-to-differ-180989520/</guid></item><item><title>研究表明霸王龙是一种温血恐龙，体温与人类相似</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/tyrannosaurus-rex-was-a-warm-blooded-dinosaur-with-a-body-temperature-similar-to-that-of-humans-study-suggests-180989519/</link><description>牙齿分析表明，这种可怕的掠食者在 97 华氏度的高温下奔跑。维持这种内部温度可能使其能够在白垩纪时期栖息在从现代阿拉斯加到墨西哥的范围内</description><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 15:59:36 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/tyrannosaurus-rex-was-a-warm-blooded-dinosaur-with-a-body-temperature-similar-to-that-of-humans-study-suggests-180989519/</guid></item><item><title>研究人员发现，一种致命动物病毒的古老 DNA 已在中世纪手稿中潜伏了几个世纪</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/medieval-manuscripts-preserved-traces-of-a-deadly-virus-for-centuries-180989522/</link><description>对牙齿和羊皮纸的一项新分析表明，毁灭性的羊痘病毒已经感染牲畜 3,700 年了</description><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 15:10:43 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/medieval-manuscripts-preserved-traces-of-a-deadly-virus-for-centuries-180989522/</guid></item><item><title>座头鲸妈妈一直陪着她死产的小鲸鱼，反复抚摸它并凝视它的眼睛。她悲伤吗？</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-humpback-whale-mom-stayed-with-her-stillborn-calf-repeatedly-touchingi-it-and-staring-into-its-eyes-was-she-grieving-180989516/</link><description>去年在澳大利亚昆士兰州海岸观察到的这一事件标志着该物种死产的首次记录，让我们难得一睹这种高度社会性的动物如何应对死亡</description><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-humpback-whale-mom-stayed-with-her-stillborn-calf-repeatedly-touchingi-it-and-staring-into-its-eyes-was-she-grieving-180989516/</guid></item><item><title>科学家创造了具有半人脑的老鼠。杂交动物可能彻底改变我们对神经系统疾病的理解</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/scientists-created-mice-with-half-human-brains-the-hybrid-animals-could-revolutionize-our-understanding-of-neurological-disorders-180989518/</link><description>众所周知，我们的大脑及其相关疾病很难研究。因此，研究人员开发了一种动物模型，其皮层（大脑的外层）是由人类细胞生长而来</description><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 20:16:55 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/scientists-created-mice-with-half-human-brains-the-hybrid-animals-could-revolutionize-our-understanding-of-neurological-disorders-180989518/</guid></item><item><title>教皇利奥十四世在梵蒂冈图书馆举办以水为主题的艺术展，庆祝他的 71 岁生日，引起轰动</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/pope-leo-xiv-makes-a-splash-for-his-71st-birthday-announcing-a-water-themed-art-exhibition-at-the-vatican-library-180989515/</link><description>当代雕塑、由印刷元素制成的鱼、具有数百年历史的论文和历史性的全球烹饪书将在新的“灾难与奇迹”艺术展中亮相</description><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 19:12:24 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/pope-leo-xiv-makes-a-splash-for-his-71st-birthday-announcing-a-water-themed-art-exhibition-at-the-vatican-library-180989515/</guid></item><item><title>这幅失传已久的格特鲁德·阿伯克龙比 (Gertrude Abercrombie) 画作在一次房地产拍卖会上以 30 美元的价格买下，现在可以卖到 25 万美元</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/bought-for-30-at-an-estate-sale-this-long-lost-gertrude-abercrombie-painting-could-now-fetch-250000-180989513/</link><description>这位来自芝加哥的超现实主义者于 1951 年创作了这件作品，然后将其送给了一位医生以换取医疗服务</description><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 18:02:16 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/bought-for-30-at-an-estate-sale-this-long-lost-gertrude-abercrombie-painting-could-now-fetch-250000-180989513/</guid></item><item><title>研究表明，数十亿年前，金星可能有一颗卫星，但金星很快就把它吞掉了</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/billions-of-years-ago-venus-may-have-had-a-moon-which-the-planet-promptly-gobbled-up-study-suggests-180989510/</link><description>科学家们一直困惑为什么这颗被称为“地球的双胞胎”的行星没有月球。计算机模拟暗示，如果金星真的有一颗，它可能会吃掉它的同伴</description><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 15:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/billions-of-years-ago-venus-may-have-had-a-moon-which-the-planet-promptly-gobbled-up-study-suggests-180989510/</guid></item><item><title>美国第一位职业女雕塑家创作的罕见大理石雕塑几十年来一直隐藏在英国花园的显眼位置</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-rare-marble-sculpture-by-americas-first-professional-female-sculptor-sat-hidden-in-plain-sight-for-decades-in-english-garden-180989508/</link><description>著名艺术家和女权主义偶像哈里特·古德休·霍斯默 (Harriet Goodhue Hosmer) 的首次半身像在房屋评估中被发现之前，一直被误认为是普通的花园装饰品</description><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 14:30:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-rare-marble-sculpture-by-americas-first-professional-female-sculptor-sat-hidden-in-plain-sight-for-decades-in-english-garden-180989508/</guid></item><item><title>研究人员分析了罗马帝国 190,000 英里的道路网。事实证明，并非所有这些都通向罗马</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/researchers-have-created-a-digital-map-of-the-roman-empires-190000-mile-network-of-roads-turns-out-not-all-of-them-led-to-rome-180989509/</link><description>在一项新的研究中，考古学家试图回答有关罗马道路的古老问题，包括首都的连接程度以及当前的高速公路是否沿着罗马路线</description><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 14:10:20 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/researchers-have-created-a-digital-map-of-the-roman-empires-190000-mile-network-of-roads-turns-out-not-all-of-them-led-to-rome-180989509/</guid></item><item><title>新西兰迎来创纪录的 90 只鸮鹦鹉雏鸟，帮助世界上最矮胖的鹦鹉物种从灭绝边缘恢复过来</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/new-zealand-welcomes-a-record-90-kakapo-chicks-helping-the-worlds-chunkiest-parrot-species-rebound-from-the-brink-of-extinction-180989511/</link><description>每年的雏鸟数量要等到最小的雏鸟达到 150 天（独立的基准）时才能确定。目前，该种群数量已达 325 只，而 1995 年为 51 只。</description><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/new-zealand-welcomes-a-record-90-kakapo-chicks-helping-the-worlds-chunkiest-parrot-species-rebound-from-the-brink-of-extinction-180989511/</guid></item><item><title>被困在恐龙粪便中的一根 6600 万年前的羽毛可能有助于解释为什么有些鸟类在大规模灭绝中幸存下来</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-66-million-year-old-feather-trapped-in-dinosaur-poop-might-help-explain-why-some-birds-survived-mass-extinction-180989496/</link><description>这块樱桃大小的粪化石于 2016 年在蒙大拿州发现，里面有羽毛、骨头以及鸟类在被兽脚亚目恐龙吃掉之前最后一餐的证据</description><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 18:45:02 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-66-million-year-old-feather-trapped-in-dinosaur-poop-might-help-explain-why-some-birds-survived-mass-extinction-180989496/</guid></item><item><title>这张新的大脑图显示了成年雄性果蝇中枢神经系统中的每个神经细胞。这就是为什么这很重要</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-new-brain-map-shows-every-nerve-cell-in-an-adult-male-fruit-flys-central-nervous-system-heres-why-that-matters-180989490/</link><description>最近发布的“连接组”与之前完成的成年雌性果蝇大脑图谱相结合。数字 3D 图使科学家能够追踪昆虫大脑中的精确神经路径，从而解开有关人类器官的秘密</description><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 16:17:14 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-new-brain-map-shows-every-nerve-cell-in-an-adult-male-fruit-flys-central-nervous-system-heres-why-that-matters-180989490/</guid></item><item><title>三只野狗穿越赞比亚打破纪录，长途跋涉超过 2,500 英里寻找伴侣</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/three-wild-dogs-made-a-record-breaking-trek-across-zambia-traveling-more-than-2500-miles-in-search-of-mates-180989505/</link><description>这些犬齿实现了非洲哺乳动物中最长的运动记录。他们的旅程凸显了保护野生动物走廊的重要性</description><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 15:47:25 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/three-wild-dogs-made-a-record-breaking-trek-across-zambia-traveling-more-than-2500-miles-in-search-of-mates-180989505/</guid></item><item><title>30多年前神秘失窃并非法运往美国，这座重300磅的雕塑终于回到法国</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/mysteriously-stolen-more-than-30-years-ago-and-illicitly-transported-to-the-us-this-300-pound-sculpture-is-finally-back-home-in-france-180989507/</link><description>阿尔弗雷德·莱佩尔 (Alfred Lepère) 的笨重作品“Faune Chasseur”再次在亚眠皮卡第博物馆展出</description><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 15:03:21 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/mysteriously-stolen-more-than-30-years-ago-and-illicitly-transported-to-the-us-this-300-pound-sculpture-is-finally-back-home-in-france-180989507/</guid></item><item><title>研究人员发现，早在 45,000 年前，塔斯马尼亚恶魔就在澳大利亚西北部与人类一起生活</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/tasmanian-devils-lived-alongside-humans-in-northwestern-australia-as-far-back-as-45000-years-ago-researchers-find-180989503/</link><description>在尤坎峡谷洞穴中出土的化石和有标记的骨头表明，这种有袋动物不仅曾经生活在该地区，而且可能是人类的“四足垃圾压实机”</description><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 13:15:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/tasmanian-devils-lived-alongside-humans-in-northwestern-australia-as-far-back-as-45000-years-ago-researchers-find-180989503/</guid></item><item><title>在足球场下几英尺处发现了一座失落已久的中世纪修道院的废墟</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-ruins-of-a-long-lost-medieval-convent-have-been-discovered-just-a-few-feet-beneath-a-soccer-field-180989506/</link><description>圣克莱尔修道院于 16 世纪关闭，研究人员认为它的所有痕迹都已丢失。但一项新的探地雷达调查显示，柱子、房间、回廊、庭院和教堂的遗迹完好无损</description><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 11:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-ruins-of-a-long-lost-medieval-convent-have-been-discovered-just-a-few-feet-beneath-a-soccer-field-180989506/</guid></item><item><title>在湾区发现了两只矮胖的山地土拨鼠。他们离家这么远在做什么？</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/marmot-mystery-how-did-these-large-mountain-dwelling-rodents-end-up-in-the-bay-area-180989502/</link><description>野生动物官员表示，本月获救的两只体型异常的啮齿动物可能搭上了一辆从山上下来的汽车的发动机舱。</description><pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 20:21:10 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/marmot-mystery-how-did-these-large-mountain-dwelling-rodents-end-up-in-the-bay-area-180989502/</guid></item></channel></rss>